-- title:
--   Node width equals the j-width of the reduced j-value
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p\ge 5$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak X$ for $p$, an algebraically closed perfect field $k$ of characteristic $p$ and a surjective ring map $red : A \to k$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with an isomorphism $eO$ onto the contraction of $A$ to the fixed field of the inertia subgroup of $A$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, with $\mathfrak m_O = (p)$, let $K$ be a fraction field of $O$ and $\iota_K : K \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ a ring map agreeing on $O$ with $eO$ followed by the inclusion of that fixed field, carrying $O$ into $A$, and let $toκ : O \to k$ be $red$ composed with $\iota_K$. Let $\mathfrak X_{reg}$ be a resolved model package for $\mathfrak X$ over $O$ with residue field $k$. Further data: ideal sheaves $Fc\,e\,k'$ on $\mathrm{Resolution}\,(p)\,e$ whose pullback along the $i$-th standard chart is generated by $V$ when $k'=i$, by $U$ when $k'=i+1$, and is the unit ideal otherwise; chart data $ch$ for $\mathfrak X_{reg}$ relative to $Fc$; integrality of the base change $\mathfrak X_O := \mathfrak X \times_{\mathbb Z} \mathrm{Spec}\,O$; a ring map $\varphi$ from the function field of $\mathfrak X_O$ to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-coefficient modular functions of level $1\cdot p$ which sends germs of constants $a \in O$ to $\iota_K(a)$ and sends the finite $j$-chart algebra to its Laurent expansions under `coeffEmb`, together with nonemptiness of that chart; and level-one place data: modular polynomial data with Kronecker congruence, integrality of the Hecke $\bar\alpha$, $\bar\beta$, a place specialization $P$, a prolongation tuple $R$ with $R$.`IsModel` (the two divisor laws and the two cusp laws), a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` consisting exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces p 1 k`, and the regularity, node-value, fixed order and value-integrality laws for $R$ on $W$. Conclusion: for every node $n$ of $\mathfrak X_{reg}$ and every $\hat j \in O$, if some element $t$ of the maximal ideal of the stalk of $\mathfrak X_O$ at the image of `𝔛reg.nodeEquiv n` under the first projection of $\mathfrak X$.`compInf k` $\times$ $\mathfrak X$.`compZero k` followed by `compInf k` followed by the base-change map along $toκ$ satisfies $\varphi(t) = j - \iota_K(\hat j)$ in the function field, then the stored width $\mathfrak X_{reg}$.`width n` equals `jWidth` of $red(\iota_K(\hat j))$, that is $3$ if this reduction is $0$, $2$ if it is $1728$, and $1$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the thickness statement for the crossings of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(p)$ in characteristic $p$: the local equation at a supersingular crossing is $uv = p^{e}$ with $e = \#\mathrm{Aut}(E)/\{\pm 1\} \in \{1,2,3\}$, read off from the reduced $j$-invariant of the crossing. It is used by the node dictionary [`ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_nodeEquiv_swap_forall_comp_eq_dict_of_sections_of_charts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_nodeEquiv_swap_forall_comp_eq_dict_of_sections_of_charts), which matches nodes of the resolved model with the supersingular place data.
